{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L138","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":138,"end":139}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":138,"end":139},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:6cc44f2bc68ecad3500ae84f3ef3ac5cc120622dbd5ad3d44a21bd899c018e42","meta":{"text":"1.2: a CASE statement. `operand` is the CASE selector (simple case `CASE x WHEN …`); a searched\ncase (`CASE WHEN cond …`) has no operand. Each branch becomes a `case-branch` condition node."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L157","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":157,"end":157}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":157,"end":157},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:07f0135d4917977cac8b753c7b2c8edeae59389d61cf277dd912fd681ae78f2b","meta":{"text":"An assignment `target := expr;`. 1.2 captures the LHS target so variable provenance is traceable."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L169","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":169,"end":169}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":169,"end":169},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:39805ee2ea77fd3c085e16216206556279a4160fed76510d867de83ad0a7c61a","meta":{"text":"A procedure/function call statement: `do_work(arg);` / `pkg.do_work(arg);`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L177","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":177,"end":179}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":177,"end":179},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:739024a68a070a7c774e1be7ed18c58c49bc9ca50768ff5ecae484548acae989","meta":{"text":"1.2: a RAISE statement. Covers both `RAISE <name>;` (a named exception) and the re-raise `RAISE;`\n(empty `name`). `RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR(code, msg)` is parsed as a raise with `name` set to\n`RAISE_APPLICATION_ERROR` and `errorCode`/`errorMessage` split out of the call args."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L192","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":192,"end":193}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":192,"end":193},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:023dea6b6e26d67ce2c1656a128a21e6a34df4b5c49d65d43d744e38037ab2ef","meta":{"text":"A statement we recognize as a statement but don't model further (e.g. NULL;, RETURN). 1.2: an\n`OPEN <cursor>` records the cursor name so an `iterates` edge can link it to the cursor node."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L206","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":206,"end":208}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":206,"end":208},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:ca3f26d05a33b47d25cfaa40d14699aa946d220e9eeec111fd597543acf8ffa6","meta":{"text":"An EXCEPTION block: `EXCEPTION WHEN <cond> THEN ... [WHEN OTHERS THEN ...]`. 1.2: now actually\ninstantiated by the parser (previously defined-but-dead); each handler becomes an\n`exception-handler` node with `whenSelector` + `handles` edges to the guarded statements."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L222","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":222,"end":222}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":222,"end":222},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:3330da947bf6b4078a591da80648430325e550fe0ca9db2723135e47ecd12946","meta":{"text":"A call site recorded on a unit/decl for cross-file `calls` resolution (extractor → resolver)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L250","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":250,"end":257}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":250,"end":257},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:a427fbfa81f112bbd7eec72f7afc578bcebfa1e7781b45811a7a98e9c69146e6","meta":{"text":"A `CREATE [OR REPLACE] TYPE [schema.]name AS OBJECT ( attr type, ... )` definition, or a\ncollection type (`AS TABLE OF <type>` / `AS VARRAY(n) OF <type>`). Object types (e.g. Oracle's\n`T_APPLICANT_CTX_OBJ`) carry a rich attribute list — the migration-relevant \"full DB context\" — so\nthe extractor surfaces them as `symbol` (type:'type') nodes with `meta.attributes`. Collections\nhave an empty attribute list and `meta.collection: { kind, elementType }` instead. A view\n(`CREATE VIEW`) reuses {@link TableDef} with `kind: 'view-ddl'`."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L269","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":269,"end":271}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":269,"end":271},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:8191e847a9e13a7e10d76946fde794cb9497bb5830205492c9277402f66988d0","meta":{"text":"A `CREATE [OR REPLACE] VIEW [schema.]name [( c1, c2, ... )] AS SELECT ...` definition. The view\nbody (the SELECT) is NOT modelled — we capture the name + optional explicit column list so the\nview is an addressable node, not silently dropped."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L281","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":281,"end":281}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":281,"end":281},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:baf420c392ccc3559399f88499a312a4c61507efe258f9284741aacc9c5f9f73","meta":{"text":"A top-level construct the parser can produce: an executable unit, a table/view DDL, or a type."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L32","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":32,"end":32}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":32,"end":32},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:5eb0dfa4195829dddff11f2ed8d65a4f4953f4896ad5599d90a226e43935bf16","meta":{"text":"A 1-based inclusive line span."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L38","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":38,"end":38}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":38,"end":38},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:ddaa2a4946cd45806d888f7e64dbd8311879dd593ce0525392d31c08a1c11912","meta":{"text":"A top-level PL/SQL unit: a package (spec/body), standalone procedure/function, or anonymous block."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L54","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":54,"end":56}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":54,"end":56},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:708103e39999da24eece43987604e06b1a999e048c7f1c82d0ca36180eb4bd98","meta":{"text":"A declaration inside a unit's declarative part: a nested procedure/function, a local variable,\nor a cursor. 1.2 adds `cursor` (CURSOR c IS SELECT …) with `cursorQuery`, and `variable` carries\n`dataType` so package-level state is recoverable for migration."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L73","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":73,"end":73}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":73,"end":73},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:66c2d701af182e521e39731dbd2359fb7248be2f0482518183d776d3660d240a","meta":{"text":"A sequence of statements that forms one lexical block. The CFG basic-block unit."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts@L79","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":79,"end":81}},"file":"packages/parsers/src/plsql/ast.ts","span":{"start":79,"end":81},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:fa89a8d880679e0b10004405e337cf2d4c67193632970d2c7a36c436095b6b98","meta":{"text":"Discriminated statement union. `sqlKind`/`expr`/`tables`/`columns` drive reads/writes edges.\n1.2 adds `CaseStmt` and `ExceptionBlock` (previously parsed-and-skipped) so guards and handlers\nsurvive into the graph."}}
